# {{ run }} — generations and judgements

Model outputs and judge verdicts produced while evaluating {{ run }}. Released so
that the reported win-rate can be re-audited without re-running training.

## Contents

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| `prompt` | Held-out prompt from `{{ cfg.data.dataset }}` |
| `policy_completion` | Sample from the trained policy |
| `baseline_completion` | Sample from the SFT baseline |
| `verdict_ab` | Judge verdict with the policy shown first |
| `verdict_ba` | Judge verdict with the order swapped |
| `score` | 1.0 win / 0.5 tie or swap-inconsistent / 0.0 loss |

## Construction

- {{ results.n_prompts if results else 'N' }} held-out prompts, never seen in SFT, RM, or policy training.
- Sampling temperature 0.7, {{ results.seeds if results else 'N' }} generation seeds.
- Every pair judged twice with positions swapped; disagreement scored as a tie
  and reported as `swap_consistency`.

## Intended use

Auditing the reported win-rate, studying judge position bias, and as a starting
point for human agreement studies. **Not** a preference-training dataset: the
labels come from an LLM judge, not from humans.
